{
 "about": "The selectors the application answers with other argument or return types than later headers of the plugin SDK declare, each with the type encoding the application's method has (answers) and the one the compiler gives the declaration of those headers (declares), on arm64 and without the frame offsets. The former SDK declares all but a few of them with the types the application has, and that surface is contract: where the two SDKs declare one selector with different types, the former declaration stands, and a plugin built with the later headers reads or passes another type there. -median and -setMedian: of ROI serve both: the double is answered with the float in its low half, and a float given is told from a double. The few the former SDK does not declare are outlets and actions the application's own nibs use with the types it has. tests/test-later-plugin-sdk-selectors.py checks that each still answers with the types recorded here, so that the list does not change unnoticed; tools/plugin-sdk-selector-sweep.py types finds it.",
